{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Mass.GammaGammaFrobeniusSelection","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Mass.GammaGammaFrobeniusSelection","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.Mass.GammaGammaVertexOrder"],"declarations":28,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.GammaGammaFrobeniusSelection.frobeniusSelected_length_eq_six","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.GammaGammaFrobeniusSelection.frobeniusSelected_length_eq_six","kind":"theorem","line":313,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/GammaGammaFrobeniusSelection.lean#L313-L322","doc":"Any reading-3-selected word on these candidates has six crossings. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.GammaGammaFrobeniusSelection.frobeniusSelected_borromean","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.GammaGammaFrobeniusSelection.frobeniusSelected_borromean","kind":"theorem","line":293,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/GammaGammaFrobeniusSelection.lean#L293-L311","doc":"**Reading 3 selects `β_Bor`**: for every `1 < q ≤ 23/20` (the proton pin is\ninside) and every Markov weight with `y_(2,1) > 0`, the minimal-crossing\nFrobenius-feasible non-zero vertex power with `k ≤ 5` is `k = 3`, the\nBorromean word. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.GammaGammaFrobeniusSelection.borromean_mem_vertexPowCands","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.GammaGammaFrobeniusSelection.borromean_mem_vertexPowCands","kind":"theorem","line":290,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/GammaGammaFrobeniusSelection.lean#L290-L291","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.GammaGammaFrobeniusSelection.vertexPowCands","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.GammaGammaFrobeniusSelection.vertexPowCands","kind":"def","line":286,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/GammaGammaFrobeniusSelection.lean#L286-L288","doc":"The candidate set: the γγ words of `H₃` with `1 ≤ k ≤ n` vertices, i.e. the\n**non-zero** vertex powers (owner ruling 2026-08-30: minimal *non-zero* feasible). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.GammaGammaFrobeniusSelection.hoefsmit_vertexPow_frobenius_table","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.GammaGammaFrobeniusSelection.hoefsmit_vertexPow_frobenius_table","kind":"theorem","line":264,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/GammaGammaFrobeniusSelection.lean#L264-L284","doc":"**The step-4 sign table as reading-3 feasibility**, for every `1 < q ≤ 23/20`\nand every weight with `y_(2,1) > 0`: `k = 1, 2, 4, 5` infeasible, `k = 3`\nfeasible. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.GammaGammaFrobeniusSelection.hoefsmitVtx_traces","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.GammaGammaFrobeniusSelection.hoefsmitVtx_traces","kind":"theorem","line":245,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/GammaGammaFrobeniusSelection.lean#L245-L262","doc":"The step-4 Chebyshev closed forms at the concrete data, `x = h²`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.GammaGammaFrobeniusSelection.hOf_sq_bounds","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.GammaGammaFrobeniusSelection.hOf_sq_bounds","kind":"theorem","line":235,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/GammaGammaFrobeniusSelection.lean#L235-L243","doc":"`0 < h² ≤ 1/10` on the interval (`h_sq_le_of_q_le` plus `h > 0`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.GammaGammaFrobeniusSelection.hoefsmit_relations","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.GammaGammaFrobeniusSelection.hoefsmit_relations","kind":"theorem","line":213,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/GammaGammaFrobeniusSelection.lean#L213-L233","doc":"The six Hoefsmit relations step 4's generic lemmas take as hypotheses, all\ndischarged from `1 < q` (as in `hoefsmit_vtx_pow_not_isHermitian`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.GammaGammaFrobeniusSelection.hoefsmitH3_vertexPow_iff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.GammaGammaFrobeniusSelection.hoefsmitH3_vertexPow_iff","kind":"theorem","line":208,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/GammaGammaFrobeniusSelection.lean#L208-L211","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.GammaGammaFrobeniusSelection.hoefsmitVtx","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.GammaGammaFrobeniusSelection.hoefsmitVtx","kind":"def","line":204,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/GammaGammaFrobeniusSelection.lean#L204-L206","doc":"The vertex image at the concrete Hoefsmit data. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.GammaGammaFrobeniusSelection.hoefsmitH3","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.GammaGammaFrobeniusSelection.hoefsmitH3","kind":"def","line":200,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/GammaGammaFrobeniusSelection.lean#L200-L202","doc":"The `H₃` block data at the concrete Hoefsmit `(2,1)` matrices of step 3. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.GammaGammaFrobeniusSelection.vertexPow_frobeniusFeasible_iff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.GammaGammaFrobeniusSelection.vertexPow_frobeniusFeasible_iff","kind":"theorem","line":185,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/GammaGammaFrobeniusSelection.lean#L185-L192","doc":"**Vertex powers**: reading-3 feasibility of `(σ₀σ₁⁻¹)^k` is the sign of the\n`(2,1)` character `tr V^k` of step 4, when the block carries positive weight. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.GammaGammaFrobeniusSelection.frobeniusSelected_nil","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.GammaGammaFrobeniusSelection.frobeniusSelected_nil","kind":"theorem","line":175,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/GammaGammaFrobeniusSelection.lean#L175-L183","doc":"As for reading 1 (`sdpSelected_nil`): with the crossing-count cost the empty\nword is reading-3-selected whenever it is a candidate. The content is in the\n*non-zero* selection below. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.GammaGammaFrobeniusSelection.nil_frobeniusFeasible","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.GammaGammaFrobeniusSelection.nil_frobeniusFeasible","kind":"theorem","line":167,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/GammaGammaFrobeniusSelection.lean#L167-L173","doc":"The empty word (the identity of `H₃`) is Frobenius-feasible: `tr 1 = 2`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.GammaGammaFrobeniusSelection.frobeniusFeasible_iff_std","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.GammaGammaFrobeniusSelection.frobeniusFeasible_iff_std","kind":"theorem","line":147,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/GammaGammaFrobeniusSelection.lean#L147-L165","doc":"**For a γγ-word, reading-3 feasibility is decided by the `(2,1)` block**: the\n`(3)` and `(1³)` characters of a γγ-word are both `1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.GammaGammaFrobeniusSelection.SDPSelected.frobenius_cost_le","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.GammaGammaFrobeniusSelection.SDPSelected.frobenius_cost_le","kind":"theorem","line":134,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/GammaGammaFrobeniusSelection.lean#L134-L139","doc":"In particular a reading-1 selection (step 1's `SDPSelected`) never undercuts a\nreading-3 selection on the same candidates and cost. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.GammaGammaFrobeniusSelection.FrobeniusSelected.cost_le_of_symPSDFeasible","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.GammaGammaFrobeniusSelection.FrobeniusSelected.cost_le_of_symPSDFeasible","kind":"theorem","line":128,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/GammaGammaFrobeniusSelection.lean#L128-L132","doc":"The reading-3 minimum is a lower bound for anything reading 2 can select. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.GammaGammaFrobeniusSelection.FrobeniusSelected.cost_le_of_psdFeasible","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.GammaGammaFrobeniusSelection.FrobeniusSelected.cost_le_of_psdFeasible","kind":"theorem","line":122,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/GammaGammaFrobeniusSelection.lean#L122-L126","doc":"The reading-3 minimum is a lower bound for anything reading 1 can select. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.GammaGammaFrobeniusSelection.FrobeniusFeasible.of_symPSDFeasible","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.GammaGammaFrobeniusSelection.FrobeniusFeasible.of_symPSDFeasible","kind":"theorem","line":114,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/GammaGammaFrobeniusSelection.lean#L114-L120","doc":"Reading 2 ⇒ reading 3: the symmetric part has trace `2 · tr (π_l w)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.GammaGammaFrobeniusSelection.FrobeniusFeasible.of_psdFeasible","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.GammaGammaFrobeniusSelection.FrobeniusFeasible.of_psdFeasible","kind":"theorem","line":109,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/GammaGammaFrobeniusSelection.lean#L109-L112","doc":"Reading 1 ⇒ reading 3: a PSD matrix has non-negative trace. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.GammaGammaFrobeniusSelection.SymPSDFeasible","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.GammaGammaFrobeniusSelection.SymPSDFeasible","kind":"def","line":105,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/GammaGammaFrobeniusSelection.lean#L105-L107","doc":"**Reading 2**: the symmetric part `π_l w + (π_l w)ᵀ` of every block is PSD. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.GammaGammaFrobeniusSelection.FrobeniusSelected.cost_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.GammaGammaFrobeniusSelection.FrobeniusSelected.cost_eq","kind":"theorem","line":91,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/GammaGammaFrobeniusSelection.lean#L91-L95","doc":"Two reading-3-selected words have equal cost. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.GammaGammaFrobeniusSelection.FrobeniusSelected.minimal","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.GammaGammaFrobeniusSelection.FrobeniusSelected.minimal","kind":"theorem","line":89,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/GammaGammaFrobeniusSelection.lean#L89-L89","doc":"No Frobenius-feasible candidate is cheaper. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.GammaGammaFrobeniusSelection.FrobeniusSelected.feasible","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.GammaGammaFrobeniusSelection.FrobeniusSelected.feasible","kind":"theorem","line":87,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/GammaGammaFrobeniusSelection.lean#L87-L87","doc":"`w` is Frobenius-feasible. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.GammaGammaFrobeniusSelection.FrobeniusSelected.mem","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.GammaGammaFrobeniusSelection.FrobeniusSelected.mem","kind":"theorem","line":85,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/GammaGammaFrobeniusSelection.lean#L85-L85","doc":"`w` is a candidate. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.GammaGammaFrobeniusSelection.FrobeniusSelected.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.GammaGammaFrobeniusSelection.FrobeniusSelected.mk","kind":"ctor","line":82,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/GammaGammaFrobeniusSelection.lean#L82-L82","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.GammaGammaFrobeniusSelection.FrobeniusSelected","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.GammaGammaFrobeniusSelection.FrobeniusSelected","kind":"structure","line":79,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/GammaGammaFrobeniusSelection.lean#L79-L89","doc":"**Reading-3 selection**: `w` is a candidate, is Frobenius-feasible, and has\nminimal cost among the Frobenius-feasible candidates. Mirror of step 1's\n`SDPSelected` with `PSDFeasible` replaced by `FrobeniusFeasible`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.GammaGammaFrobeniusSelection.FrobeniusFeasible","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.GammaGammaFrobeniusSelection.FrobeniusFeasible","kind":"def","line":73,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/GammaGammaFrobeniusSelection.lean#L73-L77","doc":"**Frobenius feasibility** (reading 3 of the confinement SDP): on every\nWedderburn block `l` with positive Markov weight `y l`, the character\n`tr (π_l w)` is non-negative. Blocks of weight `≤ 0` impose nothing. ","signatureChunk":0}]}